      "prompt_sha1": "a88edccee8028f1185c33b43c1b09c41c1210b03",
      "answer": "GPT-4 was fine-tuned using supervised learning (SFT) with demonstration data to imitate desired behavior [D3]. A reward model (RM) was trained using ranking data to predict labeler preferences, which was then used to fine-tune the SFT model via reinforcement learning (PPO algorithm) [D3]. The fine-tuning process involved training the model on a new dataset with a smaller learning rate than pre-training [W1]. This approach improved GPT-4's performance on factuality and adherence to desired behavior [D4].",
