      "answer": "Rule-based reward models (RBRMs) are a set of zero-shot GPT-4 classifiers used to provide an additional reward signal to the GPT-4 policy model during RLHF fine-tuning [D2]. They were used to steer the model towards appropriate refusals by rewarding GPT-4 for refusing harmful requests and not refusing safe ones [D3]. The RBRMs are based on rubrics for content categories and are trained using production traffic and human reviewers [D5]. This technique is related to work by Glaese et al. and Perez et al. [D3].",
